From 5fc5f40898cce79b2827ba4c7566c6b1cd0424d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:45:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: one unit per tile in cities too, with exemptions for
 aircraft and ships

Units built in an occupied city, start units, hut and barbarian units,
captures, airlifts, paradrops and units unloaded in port could stack
because only the Unit Move enabler enforced the rule. script.lua now
resolves a unit built in an occupied city at once (the better defender
stays) and sweeps the map at every turn start, relocating surplus units
to the nearest free tile: own or unowned land within 3 tiles, then 7,
then foreign land the server's teleport check accepts.

New unit flags StacksAnywhere (aircraft, helicopters, missiles) and
StacksInPort (ships, on city tiles) exempt those units, both in the Lua
count and through extra Unit Move enablers; landing from a transport
now needs an empty tile like any other move.
---
 data/civ45/README.civ45    |  19 +++-
 data/civ45/actions.ruleset |  71 +++++++++++++
 data/civ45/game.ruleset    |   3 +-
 data/civ45/script.lua      | 212 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 data/civ45/units.ruleset   |  48 +++++----
 5 files changed, 326 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/civ45/README.civ45 b/data/civ45/README.civ45
index b6262ba..e2bb068 100644
--- a/data/civ45/README.civ45
+++ b/data/civ45/README.civ45
@@ -12,9 +12,22 @@ Differences from sandbox
 ------------------------
 
 - Hex map (topology ISO|HEX) by default.
-- One unit per tile: a regular move is only legal into an empty tile
-  (MaxUnitsOnTile 0 on the "Unit Move" enabler). Boarding transports,
-  conquering cities and entering huts are separate actions and unchanged.
+- One unit per tile, cities included:
+  * A regular move or a landing from a transport is only legal into an
+    empty tile (MaxUnitsOnTile 0 on the "Unit Move" and "Transport
+    Disembark" enablers).
+  * A unit built in a city that already holds a unit is sorted out at
+    once by script.lua: the better defender stays in the city, the other
+    unit moves to the nearest free tile in its owner's territory.
+  * Every turn starts with a sweep that does the same for any other way
+    two units ended up together (start units, huts, barbarians, captures,
+    airlifts, paradrops, unloading in port).
+  * Exempt: units inside a transport; aircraft, helicopters and missiles
+    (unit flag "StacksAnywhere"), which may share any tile; ships (unit
+    flag "StacksInPort"), which may enter and share a city tile.
+  * Known limit: the move rule counts every unit, so a ship or aircraft
+    parked in a city stops a land unit from moving in. Units built there
+    still appear inside.
 - City work radius grows with the city's culture: +4 radius_sq at 300
   culture points, another +4 at 1500.
 - Cultural victory is enabled alongside spacerace and allied victory.
